    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1659-a4">

                <pb facs="1058" n="942" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg942"/>

                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Inclosures 4 and 5—Telegrams.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Consul Clare to Minister Jefferson.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Consulate</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Bluefields</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-08-16">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">August 16, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>At the request of the American and foreign interests and with hearty approval of
                    the Government officials, a party was landed from the <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Tacoma</hi> on the thirteenth. Action caused by disturbing rumors, Liberal
                    activity. Arms, ammunition are reported landed two places off the coast and now
                    supposed to be in Bluefields.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Clare</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
